      "title": "Korean batchim (final consonants) in one song! 안 알 암 앙 산 물 밤 강 #learnkorean",
      "text": "Sing along with Mongle — the Korean final consonants (batchim) ㄴ ㄹ ㅁ ㅇ in one song.\n\nA batchim sits at the bottom of a syllable:\n아 + ㄴ = 안 (an) · 아 + ㄹ = 알 (al) · 아 + ㅁ = 암 (am) · 아 + ㅇ = 앙 (ang)\nThen read real words: 산 (mountain) · 물 (water) · 밤 (chestnut / night) · 강 (river)\n손 (hand) · 눈 (snow) · 별 (star) · 말 (horse) · 곰 (bear) · 몸 (body) · 공 (ball) · 방 (room)\nㅇ on top makes no sound — shh! At the bottom it says \"ng\".\n\nTurn on English captions (CC) for the lyrics with romanization.\n\nWhich word could you read first? Comment it below 👇\n\nHangul for Beginners · 한글 초보단계 #3 — after the vowel song (#1) and the consonant song (#2).\nSYNK LAB · learn Korean the fun way, with Mongle.\n#learnkorean #hangul #batchim",
      "alt": [
        "A felt kid and the coral felt mascot Mongle build Korean syllables with a final consonant (아 + ㄴ = 안), the batchim shown in yellow, under a white card reading “Korean final consonants in one song!”"
      ],
